@startuml websocket_connection_scope_comparison
title WebSocket Connection Scope Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (Gateway protocol, exact session subscriptions)
' Source: packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/logs-chat.ts (ChatSendParamsSchema, ChatEventSchema)
' Source: src/gateway/server-broadcast.ts (createGatewayBroadcaster)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java (wireServerRoutes)
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java (handle)
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java (getOrCreate)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md (WebSocket v2 target)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/mate-chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw uses one Gateway connection for requests and events across sessions.
' Current Java behavior: one connection captures one AgentSession selected by a query parameter.
' Target-only design: Agent UI connects to a public mate-service WebSocket scoped by chat_id.
' Target-only design: mate-service opens a separate internal Runtime WebSocket scoped by session_id.
' Target-only design: public and internal connection identities, request ids, event seq, flow control, and close are independent.
' Architecture change: mate-service is a semantic gateway, not a WebSocket byte tunnel.
' Target design: RuntimeSessionStore never stores chat_id; active runs remain Pod-local.
' Design reason: separate user-facing Chat ownership from Runtime Session execution.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
left to right direction

package "OpenClaw - implemented" as openclaw {
  actor "Gateway client" as oc_client
  component "Gateway connection" as oc_conn
  component "Gateway control plane" as oc_gateway
  database "Session A" as oc_session_a
  database "Session B" as oc_session_b
  component "Node and control APIs" as oc_control

  oc_client --> oc_conn
  oc_conn --> oc_gateway : Request/Response/Event Frames
  oc_gateway --> oc_session_a : sessionKey=A
  oc_gateway --> oc_session_b : sessionKey=B
  oc_gateway --> oc_control : methods and events
}

package "pi-mono-java v1 - current" as java_v1 {
  actor "Chat client" as java_client
  component "WebSocket connection" as java_conn
  component "ChatWebSocketHandler" as java_handler
  database "AgentSession" as java_session
  database "SessionPool\nkey: conversation_id" as java_pool

  java_client --> java_conn : query conversation_id
  java_conn --> java_handler
  java_handler --> java_pool
  java_pool --> java_session
}

package "Campus two-hop target only" as campus_v2 {
  actor "Agent UI" as cc_ui
  component "Public WebSocket\nchat_id scope" as cc_public_conn
  component "mate-service\nChat semantic gateway" as cc_mate
  database "Mate Chat Store\nchat_id to session_id" as cc_chat_store
  component "Internal WebSocket\nsession_id scope" as cc_internal_conn
  component "Trusted internal gateway\nSession affinity metadata" as cc_edge
  component "ManagedSessionPool" as cc_pool
  component "ManagedRunHub" as cc_hub
  database "RuntimeSessionStore\nno chat_id" as cc_store

  cc_ui --> cc_public_conn : public Frames
  cc_public_conn --> cc_mate : one Chat
  cc_mate --> cc_chat_store : authorize and map chat_id
  cc_mate --> cc_internal_conn : rebuild Runtime Frames
  cc_internal_conn --> cc_edge : trusted session affinity
  cc_edge --> cc_pool : globally unique session_id
  cc_pool --> cc_hub : zero or one active run
  cc_pool --> cc_store : persist Runtime state
}

note bottom of openclaw
  One connection may address many sessions.
  Exact subscription, scope, and visibility filters apply.
end note

note bottom of java_v1
  Session identity is not agent-qualified.
  new_session changes the captured session.
end note

note bottom of campus_v2
  UI receives chat_id and never receives session_id.
  Agent Runtime receives session_id and never receives chat_id.
  The two WebSocket hops have independent transport state.
  Session affinity is trusted routing metadata, not an owner.
  Pod loss still interrupts an active run.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_handshake_comparison
title WebSocket Handshake and Authentication Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (Handshake, authentication, protocol versioning)
' Source: docs/gateway/clients.md (scopes, pairing, capabilities)
' Source: packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/frames.ts (ConnectParamsSchema, HelloOkSchema)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java (wireServerRoutes)
' Source: docs/asyncapi/chat-ws.yaml (query parameters and v1 messages)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/mate-chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw emits a challenge before the first client connect Request Frame.
' Current Java behavior: the route reads conversation_id and creates or resumes a session immediately.
' Target-only design: the UI authenticates and upgrades a public mate-service WebSocket before public connect.
' Target-only design: mate-service independently authenticates and upgrades an internal agent-service WebSocket.
' Target-only design: public create generates chat_id and session_id; public resume accepts only chat_id.
' Target-only design: internal connect carries session_id and never carries chat_id.
' Target-only design: trusted session-affinity metadata is derived from the authoritative mapping and validated by the internal gateway.
' Architecture change: mate-service rebuilds semantic Frames and is not a WebSocket byte tunnel.
' Design reason: Chat ownership and Runtime execution require separate authentication, routing, and failure boundaries.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
autonumber

actor "OpenClaw client" as OC
participant "OpenClaw Gateway" as OG
actor "Java v1 client" as JV1C
participant "ServerMode" as SM
participant "ChatWebSocketHandler" as CWH
actor "Agent UI" as UI
participant "mate-service\nPublic Chat endpoint" as MATE
database "Mate Chat Store" as MCS
participant "Trusted internal gateway" as EDGE
participant "agent-service\nInternal Runtime endpoint" as V2
participant "Agent and Model Managers" as MGR

== OpenClaw implemented ==
OC -> OG : WebSocket Upgrade
OG --> OC : event connect.challenge {nonce, ts}
OC -> OG : req connect {minProtocol, maxProtocol,\nauth, device, role, scopes, caps}
OG --> OC : res payload hello-ok {protocol, features,\npolicy, snapshot}
note over OC,OG
The challenge is a server event.
The first client frame is connect.
Device identity and pairing support broad Gateway access.
end note

== pi-mono-java v1 current ==
JV1C -> SM : Upgrade /api/ws/chat?conversation_id=...
SM -> CWH : handle(exchange, conversationId)
CWH --> JV1C : WebSocket accepted; no protocol hello
note over JV1C,CWH
The v1 AsyncAPI documents a token query parameter.
The baseline route shown here extracts only conversation_id.
There is no connect protocol negotiation.
end note

== Campus target: public Chat connection ==
UI -> MATE : open TLS and HTTP Upgrade\nGET /mate-service/v1/ws/chat\nuser authentication context
MATE -> MATE : authenticate user and validate Upgrade
MATE --> UI : public HTTP 101 Switching Protocols
UI -> MATE : public req connect mode=create\n{agent_id, model_id, idempotency_key}
MATE -> MCS : check idempotency and Chat quota\nvalidate user access
MATE -> MATE : guardrails, intent, and state machine
MATE -> MCS : allocate chat_id and session_id\npersist CREATING mapping

== Campus target: independent internal Runtime connection ==
MATE -> EDGE : open separate TLS and HTTP Upgrade\nGET /agent-service/internal/v1/ws/chat\nservice authentication and trusted affinity
EDGE -> EDGE : validate service identity, Upgrade,\nand session-affinity metadata
EDGE -> V2 : preserve internal principal and full path
V2 --> EDGE : accept internal Upgrade
EDGE --> MATE : internal HTTP 101 Switching Protocols
MATE -> V2 : new internal req id\nconnect mode=create\n{session_id, agent_id, model_id}
V2 -> MGR : target-audience access token\nauthorize agent and resolve model
MGR --> V2 : effective identity and model
V2 --> MATE : internal res payload\n{internal connection_id, session_id, features}
MATE -> MCS : mark mapping ACTIVE\nstore public idempotency result
MATE --> UI : public res payload\n{public connection_id, chat_id, features}
note over UI,V2
The public and internal opening handshakes return two independent 101 responses.
Each hop has its own connection_id, RequestFrame.id, EventFrame.seq,
Ping/Pong, backpressure budget, and close lifecycle.
The public Frame never exposes session_id or the internal connection identity.
The internal Frame never carries chat_id or final-user identity.
mate-service terminates both protocols and performs semantic projection.
Private keys and inbound credentials never enter Frames, Prompt, or Manager calls.
URL v1 and Frame protocol 2 are independent versions.
Public success is emitted only after internal create or resume succeeds.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_stream_recovery_comparison
title Stream and Recovery Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: src/gateway/server-chat.ts (resolveBroadcastDelta, emitChatDelta)
' Source: src/gateway/server-broadcast.ts (createGatewayBroadcaster, per-client seq, slow consumers)
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (sessions.messages.subscribe)
' Source: docs/gateway/clients.md (re-subscribe, chat.history, inFlightRun)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java (mapEventToJson, close handling)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md (ManagedRunHub)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/mate-chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw clients recover from sequence gaps by reconnecting and reloading authoritative state.
' Current Java behavior: message_update sends the accumulated message and disconnect aborts streaming.
' Target-only design: a public reconnect resumes by chat_id and mate-service resolves the authoritative session_id mapping.
' Target-only design: the internal Runtime connection resumes by session_id with trusted session-affinity metadata.
' Target-only design: public and internal connection sequences and recovery state are independent.
' Target-only design: Pool and Hub retain active-run state only inside one Pod; RuntimeSessionStore is database authority.
' Target-only design: Pod restart rebuilds the session and records interrupted history; it does not continue the active run.
' Design reason: each hop must recover independently without making a network connection the owner of a local run.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
autonumber

actor "OpenClaw client" as OC
participant "Gateway broadcaster" as OGB
participant "Chat history" as OCH
actor "Java v1 client" as JVC
participant "ChatWebSocketHandler" as JWH
participant "AgentSession" as JAS
actor "Agent UI" as UI
participant "mate-service" as MATE
database "Mate Chat Store" as MCS
participant "Trusted internal gateway" as CCG
participant "agent-service Pod A" as CCW
participant "ManagedRunHub" as MRH
database "RuntimeSessionStore" as CCH
participant "agent-service Pod B" as CCB

== OpenClaw implemented ==
OC -> OGB : sessions.messages.subscribe(sessionKey)
OGB --> OC : chat event {seq, runId, sessionKey,\ndeltaText, message?, replace?}
OGB --> OC : later event with sequence gap
OC -> OC : detect connection or run sequence gap
OC -> OCH : chat.history(sessionKey)
OCH --> OC : authoritative messages and in-flight state
note over OC,OGB
Chat delta is a standard event, not capability-gated.
Some chat deltas may be marked dropIfSlow.
A gap is observable because sequence numbers advance.
end note

== pi-mono-java v1 current ==
JAS --> JWH : MessageUpdateEvent(fullMessage, fineGrainedEvent)
JWH --> JVC : message_update {message: fullMessage}
JVC -x JWH : connection closes
JWH -> JAS : abort()
note over JVC,JAS
The wire format does not expose the fine-grained event.
There is no active-run snapshot protocol.
end note

== CampusAgent v2 target only ==
MRH --> CCW : message.updated {run_seq, typed delta}
CCW --> MATE : internal EventFrame seq=I\ncurrent delta only
MATE --> UI : public EventFrame seq=P\nprojected delta only
UI -x MATE : public connection closes
note over MRH
The internal connection and run may continue after the public connection closes.
end note

UI -> MATE : new public Upgrade and connect mode=resume {chat_id}
MATE -> MCS : authorize chat_id and resolve session_id
MCS --> MATE : session_id and trusted affinity input

alt Existing internal connection is healthy
  MATE -> CCW : keep the bound session_id connection\nsession.get and chat.history
  CCW -> CCH : read authoritative history watermark
  CCH --> CCW : messages and RunRecord state
  CCW --> MATE : Runtime snapshot and history
  MATE --> UI : public connect response and projected snapshot
else Internal connection must resume on the same Pod
  MATE -> CCG : separate internal Upgrade and resume {session_id}\nwith trusted session-affinity metadata
  CCG -> CCG : validate protected routing metadata
  CCG -> CCW : route internal path to Pod A
  CCW -> MRH : increment generation, replace old subscription,\nand atomically capture cursor
  MRH --> CCW : active_run snapshot at run_seq=N\nand history_seq=H
  CCW --> MATE : internal connect response with generation,\nfrozen config, snapshot, and cursor
  MATE -> CCW : internal chat.history(runId, through H)
  CCW -> CCH : read database history through H
  CCH --> CCW : prior messages and tool results
  CCW --> MATE : authoritative Runtime history
  MATE --> UI : new public seq and projected snapshot/history
  MRH --> CCW : deltas after N
  CCW --> MATE : ordered internal message.updated events
  MATE --> UI : independently sequenced public events
else Pod restart or routing to another Pod
  MATE -> CCG : internal resume after Pod A is unavailable
  CCG -> CCB : route to available Pod B
  CCB -> CCH : rebuild Session and Agent
  CCH --> CCB : persisted complete content blocks\nand active RunRecord
  CCB -> CCH : persist Message.status=interrupted\nand RunRecord.outcome=interrupted
  CCB --> MATE : internal connect response with active_run=null
  MATE -> CCB : internal chat.history
  CCB -> CCH : read authoritative history
  CCH --> CCB : interrupted Message and RunRecord
  CCB --> MATE : interrupted Runtime history
  MATE --> UI : public interrupted projection
end
note over UI,CCB
Public and internal connection_id, RequestFrame.id, EventFrame.seq,
Ping/Pong, backpressure, and close state are never reused across hops.
Trusted affinity is a routing hint, not a distributed run owner.
No cross-Pod active-run continuation is promised.
Unclosed tail content is not guaranteed after restart.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_transport_dependency_inversion_comparison
title WebSocket Transport Dependency Inversion Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: packages/sdk/src/types.ts (OpenClawTransport)
' Source: packages/sdk/src/transport.ts (GatewayClientTransport)
